The bug occurs when `io_wqe_create_worker()` fails to create a worker, leading to the condition where the request associated with the work item is still enqueued. The subsequent call to `goto run_cancel` attempts to cancel the request, but since it is already enqueued, it may still be executed by another worker, causing inconsistencies and resource management issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
struct io_cb_cancel_data match = {
    .fn        = io_wq_work_match_item,
    .data      = work,
    .cancel_all = false,
